ype/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477095} {:answer/id #uuid "eea57345-5cbd-5b3d-9f42-3b502e293b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eea57345-5cbd-5b3d-9f42-3b502e293b45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477096} :answer-field/id #uuid "b988546f-0744-5c59-bd81-19d25bc1359a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "097f179d-8b94-55d4-8f36-ac53f5125474" :question/math-academy-id "q-104930" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are finite?\n- **I.** $P(N)$\n- **II.** $P({Z,\\pi })$\n- **III.** $P({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The power set of a finite set is finite, while the power set of an infinite set is infinite.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Set I is infinite since the underlying set $N$ is infinite.\n\n- Set II is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\nP({Z,\\pi })={∅,\\,{Z},\\,{\\pi },\\,{Z,\\pi }}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $4.$\n\n- Set III is finite since the underlying set is finite. Notice that \n\n$$\n{x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0}={0},\n$$\n\nand, as a result, \n\n$$\nP({x\\in Z∣\\operatorname{sin}⁡x=0})=P({0})={∅,\\,{0}}\n$$\n\nhas cardinality $2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059694 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d3501b-96ef-5fbd-9d93-788021156ddb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Logically Equivalent Statements"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a475e43-ad2a-52bb-9cb1-206fb318ad0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477179} {:answer/id #uuid "f2d74735-644d-594f-8464-174d06a3e44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477180}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a475e43-ad2a-52bb-9cb1-206fb318ad0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477179} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5d89db6-f184-5558-a9c5-3c19881ea373" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477559} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "688d8a6f-9d3d-50d3-b045-b63e514e353d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477181} {:answer/id #uuid "894212aa-a160-546a-9f45-4e7ff1c222c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "894212aa-a160-546a-9f45-4e7ff1c222c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477182} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b277b4-5ed1-52b2-acfa-b00fef0f4068" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477560} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9af1a8b8-d9e6-5807-9fc8-c761158a383a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477183} {:answer/id #uuid "03a88033-d0c2-5192-ac1b-264d0b7c2da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477184}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9af1a8b8-d9e6-5807-9fc8-c761158a383a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477183} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8c3534b-c88f-5cd8-a830-dd021584e964" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477561}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37ad276a-88ce-596c-9a24-406a32aa6e25" :question/math-academy-id "q-171334" :question/problem "$\\,$ **If** $10\\ge 1,$ **then** $3\\in R.$ \n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n- **I.** If $10<1,$ then $3\\notin R.$\n- **II.** If $3\\notin R,$ then $10<1.$\n- **III.** If $3\\in R,$ then $10\\ge 1.$\n\nCompare the logical forms for arbitrary truth values of the antecedent and consequent.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement II is the contrapositive. $\\,✓$\n\n- Statement III is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064612 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064163 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e901ea71-aeab-5e95-939e-2401558aa708" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Global Extrema of a Function on a Given Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fffa006c-260c-5be0-86f5-b6b545e204c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477197} {:answer/id #uuid "103f92cc-ed66-5df8-b5ca-639e6c09ce4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "103f92cc-ed66-5df8-b5ca-639e6c09ce4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477198} :answer-field/id #uuid "85a48273-f59a-5b72-9eea-30c67eba5b6c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477568} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0a3ef07-c7ae-5f79-a278-96cf3a6afeb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477199} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf09ba6-a8e3-5984-a169-e863ad9ec44b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0a3ef07-c7ae-5f79-a278-96cf3a6afeb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477199} :answer-field/id #uuid "b487b83d-f170-53d4-a600-612f5bb14a90" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477569} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7075c86b-5a37-5b8a-9198-9df0fae9f1ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477201} {:answer/id #uuid "28638f72-40f2-5e2a-b417-e7841b921eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477202}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28638f72-40f2-5e2a-b417-e7841b921eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477202} :answer-field/id #uuid "d89d5c80-1038-555d-85ba-6e8abe9bb00b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477570}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "542cb4a0-6380-5eaf-91e8-44f9300f10c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-22428" :question/problem "For the function $f(x)=x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ defined on the closed interval $\\frac{1}{2}\\le x\\le e,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The global maximum value is $\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$\nII. The global minimum value is $e-2$\nIII. The global minimum value is $2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Let's apply the candidates test step by step.\n\n**Step 1**: We find the critical points. Taking the derivative of $f(x)=x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ we get\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=1-\\frac{2}{x},\n$$\n\nand solving ${f}^{′}(x)=0,$ we get \n\n$$\n1-\\frac{2}{x}=0\\,⟹\\,x=2.\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=2,$ and the endpoints $x=\\frac{1}{2},e$ (since the derivative is not defined at the endpoints).\n\n**Step 2**: We evaluate $f(x)$ at the critical points.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\frac{1}{2}) & =\\frac{1}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2≈1.9 \\\\ f(2) & =2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2≈0.6 \\\\ f(e) & =e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e=e-2≈0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: We compare all of the values found in step $2.$\n\n- The greatest value is $f(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ so the global maximum is $\\frac{1}{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\n- The smallest value is $f(2)=2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ so the global minimum is $2-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is, \"I and III only.\"\n\n![](images/6c/6cc3ee476c8c5dc9e27051c990b184318147caffd2177b760074172fe5c667f6.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Transformations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed20dcfb-93aa-5edf-8467-1766b4b4b822" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477473} {:answer/id #uuid "d32af6f8-8b0f-5234-806c-62e9d747df5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d32af6f8-8b0f-5234-806c-62e9d747df5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477474} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c20384a-0816-5afd-a2d2-3cd169248491" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93078b9b-9d6c-5f09-8800-51a8a1ec8bbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477475} {:answer/id #uuid "2ea56d0c-ed1c-5b1a-8bbd-91e911ada20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ea56d0c-ed1c-5b1a-8bbd-91e911ada20d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477476} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdecd740-b0ed-58be-95a9-c0e256d73db9" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4df3c9b-0f75-5bb2-b7f3-076984d785f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477477} {:answer/id #uuid "f15219cd-4112-5f94-bd53-1aa374fbf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f15219cd-4112-5f94-bd53-1aa374fbf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477478} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c819544-8a99-529a-8823-7309e6fe05a9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a9a96319-3bb3-5dd4-a3ac-27f5effab07d" :question/math-academy-id "q-8331" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\nII. $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\nIII. $T$ is a linear transformation\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}ky \\\\ kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}y \\\\ x\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}+{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ac97073-f2e4-57fa-bc98-21619911b032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477307} {:answer/id #uuid "fed5ba5b-9655-57ac-bf85-e26d4ca80ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fed5ba5b-9655-57ac-bf85-e26d4ca80ab6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477308} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9a32b98-4ce8-5ab9-ba0f-52336fc8a891" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab354b54-184d-5e28-ab49-c725761e84d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477309} {:answer/id #uuid "5f7c4fb6-9856-5e08-8e95-baf50093e535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477310}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f7c4fb6-9856-5e08-8e95-baf50093e535" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477310} :answer-field/id #uuid "579c28da-6262-519a-b610-6fec803beaf2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477624} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f8cc3b1-c6eb-5129-bcad-4e7d08d4a6cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477311} {:answer/id #uuid "88d68881-4ce5-5cc2-8b8b-c3129b170191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88d68881-4ce5-5cc2-8b8b-c3129b170191" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477312} :answer-field/id #uuid "058434be-b274-586d-9c20-7a526c76c9a3" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477625}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59f14d04-9b7d-5b14-8363-a42027c3b11c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42374" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 & 1 & 7 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -0 & 6\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statement are true regarding the matrices $A,B,$ and $C?$\n\nI. The product $AB$ is well defined\nII. The product $BA$ is well defined\nIII. The product $AC$ is well defined\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $A$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $B.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $B,$ the matrices $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 4}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $B$ and $4$ rows in $A.$ Since the number of columns in $B$ equals the number of rows in $A,$ the matrices $B$ and $A$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{B}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{✓}{A}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $2$ columns in $A$ and $2$ rows in $C.$ Since the number of columns in $A$ equals the number of rows in $C,$ the matrices $A$ and $C$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{4\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{✓}{C}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that all three statements are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106052 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105861 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16a6f0f7-4003-5908-8b1b-68d218fdcb8f" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is a Valid PDF"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d92691-4283-5860-99ee-02d2c7eaa522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477139} {:answer/id #uuid "3c825ee0-9652-5761-9331-e690af0d02e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16d92691-4283-5860-99ee-02d2c7eaa522" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477139} :answer-field/id #uuid "24acb4e9-34d2-5789-95a2-7572c55719a6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477539} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc92b194-f3a4-5cf2-bc00-85b12e02a5dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477141} {:answer/id #uuid "29f6623d-5845-5d90-a644-3e3d85f2e27b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477142}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29f6623d-5845-5d90-a644-3e3d85f2e27b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477142} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8355a43-db9c-512b-999c-b01ab07d71f8" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477540} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02a46a15-e35a-5d37-809a-52dbc532a817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477143} {:answer/id #uuid "61c8aa07-a26f-5be9-a6a5-d571ab98ecbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477144}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02a46a15-e35a-5d37-809a-52dbc532a817" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477143} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0f0e01e-4467-5c13-8c4d-bf4a4eac9f08" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ed6c6ac-3d65-5bdf-b16d-eef1fafdf163" :question/math-academy-id "q-154690" :question/problem "![](images/f2/f299f0d25bfee9303a6485413d44f1a6ce7b863c79ccae91f4f8d5d604f2bac3.png)\n\nConsider the function $f(x)$ whose graph is shown above.\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x-1}{4},\\, & 0\\le x<4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [0,4)$\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is a valid probability density function\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "For a function $f(x)$ to be a valid probability density function on a set $S,$ it must satisfy the following conditions:\n\n- $f(x)\\ge 0$ for all $x$\n\n- ${\\int }_{S}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1$\n\nNow, let's consider each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. $f(x)$ is negative for some values of $x.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{x-1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x-1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-x]}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}([\\frac{16}{2}-4]-[\\frac{0}{2}-0]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(8-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement I is false, $f(x)$ is not a valid probability density function.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106216 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105755 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0d25a77b-7977-50b2-b375-51b8539bc9b9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Type of a Polygon"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e69e1d5d-0656-5c9a-ba41-e8cea1efbe8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477203} {:answer/id #uuid "6afe4f0c-9313-57f5-b369-4756d7b902fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e69e1d5d-0656-5c9a-ba41-e8cea1efbe8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477203} :answer-field/id #uuid "15486f8e-a86e-5074-b47e-382a17c9bc4f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477571} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e5d2a80-b1c4-5de8-93eb-93d42ffa3a06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477205} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd2494c-cda5-507c-a617-eb1aaf9d195d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd2494c-cda5-507c-a617-eb1aaf9d195d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477206} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fcfaea9-4e0b-55f7-9744-097c3e26ac6f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477572} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bed70861-52aa-58b4-8f05-a3569a02d575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477207} {:answer/id #uuid "8917533b-727d-53ee-b0d2-eff35cd63763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477208}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bed70861-52aa-58b4-8f05-a3569a02d575" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477207} :answer-field/id #uuid "fae5ae97-5a74-5251-b85f-fe579c7a5170" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18613fbc-efad-5e39-8673-d89aa94c710c" :question/math-academy-id "q-236888" :question/problem "![](images/10/102620aa55d15a8c07dc8224fd4de06d91cbd2abbbde6ee812df85a4862dc566.png)\n\nWhich of the above polygons are complex?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A polygon is **simple** if its boundary does not intersect itself. Otherwise, the polygon is called **complex**.\n\nAmong the given polygons, only polygon II has intersecting sides. \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106297 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32467c2c-5605-50e9-b961-a29535a0effb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fa458c3-7282-53ea-a5bc-e0d9c9649ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477265} {:answer/id #uuid "6323e003-b566-54fd-8ad4-a54a9bcf1cc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9fa458c3-7282-53ea-a5bc-e0d9c9649ae4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477265} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ff5f153-df81-5564-84ec-df4c0c2a6cb4" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477602} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "927430a2-7643-57f4-820b-091a125a9885" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477267} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb94d42-b075-53e5-a318-c0b8c764abd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9bb94d42-b075-53e5-a318-c0b8c764abd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477268} :answer-field/id #uuid "783247a3-0ebe-54a6-98ea-9862b85cfe12" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "514a35aa-74e7-586d-b428-f5e95b6fdef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477269} {:answer/id #uuid "aec979f1-be2c-5a54-b2f4-f82b778d6eaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "514a35aa-74e7-586d-b428-f5e95b6fdef4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477269} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8624b7d-1161-5bdc-b93a-f2003b597423" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2b717856-6a11-5857-bbda-def4fc991b4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-36792" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** $v=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2.$\n- **II.** $v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ is an eigenvector of $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}]$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =0.$\n- **III.** If $v$ is an eigenvector of a matrix $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =2,$ then $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ corresponding to $\\lambda =6.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the eigenvectors of $A$ are the non-zero vectors $v$ such that $Av=\\lambda v.$ With that in mind, let's examine the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Av & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =1$ (but not $2$).\n\n- Statement II is true. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{v}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSince $Av=0v,$ we conclude that $v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(3v)=3Av=3(2v)=2(3v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince, $A(3v)=2(3v),$ and $3v\\ne 0,$ this implies that $3v$ is an eigenvector of $A$ and the corresponding eigenvalue is $\\lambda =2$ (but not $6$).\n\n**Note:** In general, any non-zero multiple of an eigenvector is again an eigenvector, and the corresponding eigenvalue is the same.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110674 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f67c3319-1153-51ed-a57a-f85c06c7e76c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Points on Intersecting Lines Are Collinear"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "971706ed-5d46-504e-aa