eckbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f1bdc4c9-5c09-5a10-a62f-cd8a566a9012" :question/math-academy-id "q-42438" :question/problem "Which of the following values lies in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x?$\n\nI. $\\sqrt{3}$\nII. $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\nIII. $99\\,999$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/d7/d7984b9098d02bfc2b1e9a422aef919533abce54fbb94117e709c7613b0870a3.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, all the given values are in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111260 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00889b75-3745-52f6-9157-912846482689" :knowledge-point/title "Describing a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d947ac2e-b8fe-5bf6-bc0d-bd8ae09130fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477347} {:answer/id #uuid "51e54763-10f4-58f1-b051-1f618f62eaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "51e54763-10f4-58f1-b051-1f618f62eaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477348} :answer-field/id #uuid "0eee5ecf-7db6-51d4-95a6-a232b1c8d80b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a46e7c96-e1e6-5fb5-b22b-883c33a3c731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477349} {:answer/id #uuid "c4196612-ccb5-53b4-9e62-44b13bdc859f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4196612-ccb5-53b4-9e62-44b13bdc859f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477350} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1ebfaf3-1af3-515a-ab19-6144fb13df92" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477644} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82de10d3-76ce-5fc3-b275-3168f31a74f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477351} {:answer/id #uuid "d31e4384-7b72-540a-9f5d-372195b98996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82de10d3-76ce-5fc3-b275-3168f31a74f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477351} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8a46a7b-599a-5c9b-bddd-9358f4dbbba0" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477645}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "599179be-ddc2-50ab-a431-64168ebbcf12" :question/math-academy-id "q-53000" :question/problem "![](images/6b/6bffbc53c9e35da03655638ca40c5899bc5290cbadf3d14aef8e82585f14e004.png)\n\nWhich of the following terms describe the shape above?\n\nI. Kite\n\nII. Rectangle\n\nIII. Trapezoid\n\nUse the convention that a kite has at least two pairs of equal adjacent sides and a trapezoid has exactly one pair of parallel sides.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nLet's now look at the terms one by one.\n\n- The given figure is a quadrilateral with two pairs of congruent sides that are adjacent to each other, so it is a kite.\n\n- Since the four angles of the quadrilateral are right angles, it is a rectangle.\n\n- The quadrilateral has two pairs of opposite sides that are parallel to each other, not one pair. So it is **not** a trapezoid.\n\nConsequently, the given shape is described by terms I (kite), and II (rectangle)."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111262 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110778 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "34ed7bcd-3c06-592e-906c-5010e80370db" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Quadrilaterals"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e8af694-f9ab-5243-92cd-ee16bcb00f53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477353} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f82d28-0dda-5a10-a974-9a87aef74dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3f82d28-0dda-5a10-a974-9a87aef74dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477354} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8ffdb2a-36e3-5f56-bd99-527b102cbbbc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477646} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f111530a-98a7-5bd5-ae40-2760bcbe73c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477355} {:answer/id #uuid "fe6a353f-0be7-552a-b591-45c60421393f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe6a353f-0be7-552a-b591-45c60421393f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477356} :answer-field/id #uuid "babaeecd-6a33-5cff-812a-06f3b54955a1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477647} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22ec773a-7124-539e-ae98-4f4dcca6ddff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477357} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9b4b1c-1ba6-5907-baad-e342f1982ac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "22ec773a-7124-539e-ae98-4f4dcca6ddff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477357} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff4d475d-6602-5dcb-b458-27e16262b216" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5c9c084b-0547-549b-b2ae-ba90597387ae" :question/math-academy-id "q-53010" :question/problem "![](images/b6/b68f8d3d0634999697051b668c06dd34c1191905a7bebda79925cd437d454d36.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the trapezoid above?\n\nI. $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$\n\nII. $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}.$\n\nIII. $\\overset{―}{AD}∥\\overset{―}{BC}.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. The trapezoid has a pair of parallel sides, $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$\n\n- Statement II is true. We can see that $∠ABC$ is a right angle, that is, $m∠ABC={90}^{∘}.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The trapezoid has one pair of parallel sides, $\\overset{―}{AB}∥\\overset{―}{CD}.$ We can see that $\\overset{―}{AD}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$ are not parallel.\n\nIn conclusion, statements I and II are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111356 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e99a9025-fb5a-54a5-9ab7-72135a77225a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477371} {:answer/id #uuid "31d95762-28dc-50a8-9be3-b41da2513393" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e99a9025-fb5a-54a5-9ab7-72135a77225a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477371} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebe38af3-d0d5-5d75-8290-3d1c253f0e72" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a190686-8589-5b4f-bc1a-09311cd52f78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477373} {:answer/id #uuid "ab355908-fb0d-548d-91e1-477450397db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab355908-fb0d-548d-91e1-477450397db4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477374} :answer-field/id #uuid "020c5de8-ab36-5db9-93c8-08f5b80d9611" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05fb94e2-3269-55ad-b4e5-f2eae77367f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477375} {:answer/id #uuid "e76f3778-f579-5d7f-8eb5-1903f27e06d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05fb94e2-3269-55ad-b4e5-f2eae77367f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477375} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c0ede3e-962d-534c-8407-ad55a5311589" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "183017f0-e71f-5632-89e1-4603485e8f26" :question/math-academy-id "q-65744" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\nI. $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{2})$\nII. $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\nIII. $(0,2\\pi )$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{6})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{1}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\pi }{3},\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(0,2\\pi ).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(2\\pi ,0)$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=2\\pi $ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(0,2\\pi )$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186111361 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110575 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "af0b18ca-54a2-5a24-a670-faa311096abc" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56708daa-2130-56c2-b5e5-0e10fce06ad0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477377} {:answer/id #uuid "069f7725-2ffb-56bc-b017-8a08b698c7d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477378}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56708daa-2130-56c2-b5e5-